! NiI2 monolayer, spin-spiral SCF -- the pw.x form of the Elk input.
!
! Elk -> defumat, term by term:
!
!   avec (bohr)          -> ibrav = 4 (hexagonal): a1 = (a,0,0),
!                           a2 = (-a/2, a*sqrt(3)/2, 0), a3 = (0,0,c), which is
!                           Elk's matrix exactly. celldm(1) = 7.360483 bohr,
!                           celldm(3) = 46.255853/7.360483 = 6.2843502254.
!   atoms / atposl       -> ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal). The trailing three zeros
!                           on each Elk position line are bfcmt (a per-atom field)
!                           and are zero, so nothing is carried over.
!   spinsprl + vqlss     -> noncolin = .true. + spiral_q, in lattice coordinates,
!                           which is the same convention as vqlss.
!   ngridk 9 9 1         -> K_POINTS automatic 9 9 1 0 0 0. nosym = .true. is
!                           mandatory: the spin space group is not implemented,
!                           so a spiral runs the full 81-point grid.
!   bfieldc 0.05 0 0     -> deliberately NOT reproduced. In Elk that field is a
!                           transverse seed that breaks spin symmetry so the
!                           spiral can form; here starting_magnetization with
!                           angle1 = 90 does the same job and stays out of the
!                           total energy. An external field's energy is excluded
!                           from the reported total by convention (P18), so
!                           carrying it would contaminate the E(q) differences
!                           this calculation is for.
!   rgkmax/gmaxvr/lmaxapw-> LAPW basis knobs with no plane-wave counterpart. The
!                           cutoff comes from the pseudopotentials instead.
!   epspot 1e-7          -> conv_thr (on the density, Ry).
!
! starting_magnetization is a fraction of the *valence* charge, and this Ni
! carries eighteen valence electrons (3s 3p semicore), so the usual "0.4" would
! seed 7.2 Bohr magnetons on an ion whose moment is about 2. 0.15 x 18 = 2.7 is
! the seed, verified by integrating the starting density: channel 0 gives 52.0
! electrons and channel 1 (m_x, since angle1 = 90) gives 2.7, m_y = m_z = 0.
!   mixtype 3 (Broyden)  -> the default mixer here is Broyden.
!
! Pseudopotentials: SG15 ONCV PBE-1.2, norm-conserving and *scalar*-relativistic.
! Norm-conserving because a spiral refuses ultrasoft and PAW; scalar because a
! fully-relativistic dataset without lspinorb is refused (average_pp is not
! implemented) and lspinorb breaks the generalized Bloch theorem outright.
! Ni carries 18 valence electrons (3s 3p 3d 4s) and I 17 (4d 5s 5p): 52 in all.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    prefix = 'nii2'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 4, celldm(1) = 7.360483, celldm(3) = 6.2843502254,
    nat = 3, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 80.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.01,
    nbnd = 64,
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.15
    angle1(1) = 90.0
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.0
    angle1(2) = 90.0
    spiral_q(1) = 0.0, spiral_q(2) = 0.0, spiral_q(3) = 0.0
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8
    electron_maxstep = 200
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Ni  58.693  Ni.pbe-nc-sg15.UPF
 I  126.904  I.pbe-nc-sg15.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 Ni  0.00000000000  0.00000000000  0.0000000
 I   0.33333333333  0.66666666667  0.0615401
 I   0.66666666667  0.33333333333  0.9384599
K_POINTS {automatic}
 9 9 1 0 0 0
